# Line endings: LF everywhere, Windows included.
#
# This is not a style preference — it is load-bearing. Several tests read
# source files as TEXT and assert on their exact bytes:
#
#   * src/firstRunExperience.test.mjs SHA-256s the GEV_REALTIME_TOOLS block
#     and pins its exact byte length. Measured under a CRLF checkout, that
#     block grows 622 bytes (one per line) and hashes to something else.
#   * src/scenes/director.test.mjs probes ui.js with a regex terminated by
#     "\n  }\n". CRLF puts "\r" before that newline, so the match returns null
#     and the test reports the method as "missing from ui.js".
#   * src/layerShedding.test.mjs and others anchor on "\n" the same way.
#
# A CRLF checkout therefore fails ~25 tests that have nothing wrong with them,
# on Windows only, with error messages that all point at the wrong thing.
# src/lineEndings.test.mjs guards this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4 binary
*.glb binary
*.gltf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
